# CyberGuard custom detection rules (source of truth).
# Deployed on the Kali VM to /var/lib/suricata/rules/cyberguard.rules.
# Local custom SID range (>= 1000000) avoids clashing with vendor-shipped rules.
# Do not reformat or wrap the rule lines.
#
# rev:2 (Phase 5) adds priority + classtype so alerts carry a real severity and
# category. PENDING KALI VALIDATION: these edits have NOT yet been validated on
# the VM — run `sudo suricata -T -c /etc/suricata/suricata.yaml -v` and the lab
# tests on Kali to confirm they load and fire before relying on them.
#
# sid 1000001 — "CyberGuard Test Alert"
#   Fires on an HTTP request to a server (established flow) whose URI contains
#   "/cyberguard-test". priority:1 => severity 1 (Critical). classtype:misc-activity.
alert http any any -> any any (msg:"CyberGuard Test Alert"; flow:to_server,established; http.uri; content:"/cyberguard-test"; priority:1; classtype:misc-activity; sid:1000001; rev:2;)
#
# sid 1000002 — "CyberGuard Warning Alert"
#   Fires on an HTTP request to a server (established flow) whose URI contains
#   "/cyberguard-warning". priority:2 => severity 2 (High). classtype:misc-activity.
alert http any any -> any any (msg:"CyberGuard Warning Alert"; flow:to_server,established; http.uri; content:"/cyberguard-warning"; priority:2; classtype:misc-activity; sid:1000002; rev:2;)
